reated on both node1 and node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"id dataops on both nodes shows uid=4500(dataops) gid=4500(dataops), created via addgroup -g 4500 / adduser -u 4500.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e3addc2da5764bb4\",\"cmd-cd08d2c064d74f99\"]},{\"id\":\"directory-ownership-mode\",\"requirement\":\"Shared directory /srv/nfs/shared set to dataops:dataops mode 2770\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"ls -lad on node1 shows drwxrws--- dataops dataops immediately after chmod 2770; the same mode/ownership is visible on the node2 mount, confirming the setting propagates over NFS.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4fad39065f7f4d27\",\"cmd-b2e79a066035460c\"]},{\"id\":\"nfs-export-node1\",\"requirement\":\"node1 exports /srv/nfs/shared via NFS\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"/etc/exports configured, rpcbind and nfs services started successfully, exportfs -v confirms the export scoped to node2's IP, and post-restart checks show the export and service still active.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-789de224fc024bd0\",\"cmd-23b2c00eb6c84930\",\"cmd-afc3267cfd74490d\",\"cmd-fc003ab507364abf\",\"cmd-f8c1d66cc92f4e03\"]},{\"id\":\"mount-node2\",\"requirement\":\"node2 mounts the export at /mnt/shared\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"mount output on node2 shows an active nfs4 mount of 10.100.163.10:/srv/nfs/shared at /mnt/shared with correct ownership/mode; fstab entry with _netdev added for persistence, and the mount is confirmed functional both immediately and (after a discovered netmount runlevel gap was fixed) automatically on subsequent reboots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-314a2b47ccb24486\",\"cmd-b2e79a066035460c\",\"cmd-db76250556d241b4\"]},{\"id\":\"cross-node-consistency\",\"requirement\":\"Files created on either system retain consistent dataops:dataops ownership and 2770 permissions when viewed from the other side\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A file created as dataops on node1 (from-node1.txt) is visible with dataops:dataops ownership from node2, and a file created as dataops via the node2 mount (from-node2.txt) is visible with the same ownership from node1's local view of /srv/nfs/shared.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0642a7a009224999\",\"cmd-aa334ae72c2c4651\",\"cmd-2dceb310b67b449a\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Command trace is largely clean: discovery, package installs, user/group creation, export/mount configuration, and verification steps all map directly to the task or to the mandatory restart-evidence protocol. The netmount runlevel fix on node2 (cmd-3ae40e2d0c944f3e) was a legitimate corrective action addressing a genuine persistence gap discovered during the restart protocol, not an unrelated experiment, and it was validated with a second restart. The only residue is two small reboot scheduler log files (/tmp/reboot.log, /tmp/reboot2.log) left on node1 and node2 respectively, visible in the after-executor temporary-files diff; these are low-risk, bounded artifacts of the restart mechanism itself and were not cleaned up.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3ae40e2d0c944f3e\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task contract are satisfied with direct, first-hand evidence: dataops (UID/GID 4500) exists on both nodes, /srv/nfs/shared on node1 is dataops:dataops mode 2770 and exported via NFS, node2 mounts it at /mnt/shared with matching ownership/mode, and cross-node file creation preserves consistent ownership in both directions. The executor additionally ran the mandatory node-restart protocol on both nodes, capturing pre-restart boot identity/health, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery for both node1 and node2; it discovered that node2's NFS mount did not survive a reboot because the netmount OpenRC service was not enabled in the default runlevel, fixed it, and validated the fix with a second full restart cycle showing automatic remount and intact data.\",\"limitations\":[\"The netmount persistence gap on node2 was only discovered because the executor performed the restart protocol; had it not been run, the task's underlying mount-at-boot persistence would have gone unverified (though this is not itself part of the stated task contract).\",\"Two small reboot-scheduler log files (/tmp/reboot.log on node1, /tmp/reboot.log and /tmp/reboot2.log on node2) were left behind and not cleaned up, a minor hygiene item.\",\"Directory listing permission checks (e.g., cmd-aa334ae72c2c4651) show 'Permission denied' for the default (non-dataops) execution user against the 2770 directory, which is expected behavior given the restrictive mode and not a fault, but it means the raw command output alone is slightly ambiguous without the follow-up sudo -u dataops verification.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"dataops-identity","requirement":"Shared identity 'dataops' with UID/GID 4500 created on both node1 and node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"id dataops on both nodes shows uid=4500(dataops) gid=4500(dataops), created via addgroup -g 4500 / adduser -u 4500.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e3addc2da5764bb4","cmd-cd08d2c064d74f99"]},{"id":"directory-ownership-mode","requirement":"Shared directory /srv/nfs/shared set to dataops:dataops mode 2770","status":"satisfied","summary":"ls -lad on node1 shows drwxrws--- dataops dataops immediately after chmod 2770; the same mode/ownership is visible on the node2 mount, confirming the setting propagates over NFS.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4fad39065f7f4d27","cmd-b2e79a066035460c"]},{"id":"nfs-export-node1","requirement":"node1 exports /srv/nfs/shared via NFS","status":"satisfied","summary":"/etc/exports configured, rpcbind and nfs services started successfully, exportfs -v confirms the export scoped to node2's IP, and post-restart checks show the export and service still active.","evidence_ids":["cmd-789de224fc024bd0","cmd-23b2c00eb6c84930","cmd-af