ary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task contract are satisfied with direct, first-hand evidence: dataops (UID/GID 4500) exists on both nodes, /srv/nfs/shared on node1 is dataops:dataops mode 2770 and exported via NFS, node2 mounts it at /mnt/shared with matching ownership/mode, and cross-node file creation preserves consistent ownership in both directions. The executor additionally ran the mandatory node-restart protocol on both nodes, capturing pre-restart boot identity/health, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery for both node1 and node2; it discovered that node2's NFS mount did not survive a reboot because the netmount OpenRC service was not enabled in the default runlevel, fixed it, and validated the fix with a second full restart cycle showing automatic remount and intact data.","limitations":["The netmount persistence gap on node2 was only discovered because the executor performed the restart protocol; had it not been run, the task's underlying mount-at-boot persistence would have gone unverified (though this is not itself part of the stated task contract).","Two small reboot-scheduler log files (/tmp/reboot.log on node1, /tmp/reboot.log and /tmp/reboot2.log on node2) were left behind and not cleaned up, a minor hygiene item.","Directory listing permission checks (e.g., cmd-aa334ae72c2c4651) show 'Permission denied' for the default (non-dataops) execution user against the 2770 directory, which is expected behavior given the restrictive mode and not a fault, but it means the raw command output alone is slightly ambiguous without the follow-up sudo -u dataops verification."]},"ttft_ms":30062,"type":"result","duration_ms":67280,"uuid":"ca199f10-9a4b-48d4-ad4a-fa837278c52a","ttft_stream_ms":1086,"time_to_request_ms":38,"queued_turn_count":0}
